-# Reusable: weekly develop-to-main promotion pull request.
+# Reusable: daily green-to-main promotion pull request.
 #
-# Opens a pull request from develop into main when develop has commits that main
-# does not and no open promotion pull request exists. The pull request carries the
-# release:in-progress label that _release-freeze.yml reads. Auto-merge is never
-# enabled.
+# Stops (with an ntfy post when configured) when main has commits that develop
+# lacks, since promoting would revert them. Otherwise dispatches the caller's
+# full-suite workflow on the green branch, waits for it to succeed, creates a
+# promote/<yyyy-mm-dd> branch at the tested sha, opens the pull request into
+# main, and arms merge-commit auto-merge on it.
 #
 # The pull request is opened with the release GitHub App token, not github.token,
 # so the pull_request workflows run on it.
@@ -11,20 +12,37 @@
 # Caller shape:
